sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: VM CI (verifying-commands skill, "Run the same proof in development and CI"), docs/reference/feature-flow.md "The VM job", swamp/proof/reset/README.md, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: proof:run
  %% kind: proof.run
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant S as Proof VM<br/>task VM over ssh
  CLI->>GW: proof:run COMMIT
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit proof:run COMMIT`
  %%> - syntax: `<commit> [--all] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the full commit SHA and nothing else; Orbit selects the cases itself
  Note over GW: Check the commit<br/>branch head or approved PR
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to the Gateway Node
  %%> - the SHA is a full lowercase SHA that the Orbit repository has
  %%> - the commit is the head of a branch of the Orbit repository
  %%> - or it is the head of an open pull request from elsewhere that carries the label `run-proofs` and has an approving review of exactly that commit from a maintainer
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a pull request from outside can carry any code; Orbit runs it only after a maintainer approved that exact commit
  %%> - the Gateway reads GitHub with its App token and fetches no code here
  Note over GW: Select the cases<br/>diff · selection list
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - lists the files that differ between the commit and its merge base with `main`
  %%> - maps each path with the selection list of the commit; the last matching line wins
  %%> - selects every case when the selection list changed or the file list is incomplete
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the selected case programs, and the paths that no case covers
  alt refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>proof.commit_untrusted
    %%> When:
    %%> - the commit is not trusted (`proof.commit_untrusted`) or unknown (`proof.commit_not_found`)
    %%> - a changed path matches no line of the selection list (`proof.path_unmapped`)
    %%> - the calling Node has no access grant (`node_access.required`)
    %%> - GitHub cannot be read, so the commit or its diff cannot be checked (`proof.github_unavailable`)
    %%> - the selection list is malformed (`proof.selection_invalid`)
    %%> - cases are selected and proof execution is switched off (`proof.execution_disabled`): the error holds the selected cases and the uncovered paths
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded and nothing starts
  else nothing to prove
    GW-->>CLI: Skipped — nothing to prove<br/>proof.nothing_to_prove
    %%> Result:
    %%> - only paths that need no proof changed, such as documentation and charts
    %%> - no group is created and nothing runs
    %%> - the task is recorded as succeeded, with no run
    %%> - paths marked as having no case yet are listed in the result
  else cases selected
    Note over GW: Open the proof group<br/>Project 46 · tasks:create
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates a task group on the Orbit Project with one review subtask, as `tasks:create` does
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - proof execution is switched on (`ORBIT_PROOF_RUN_EXECUTION`)
    Note over GW: Provision at the commit<br/>tasks.provision
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - admits `tasks.provision` for the group; its workspace starts exactly at the commit, not at the newest green commit
    %%> - the VM is the regular task VM of today, with the Pi token and model key that every task VM carries
    %%> When it waits:
    %%> - no host has room: the provision waits (`capacity`), as for any task
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the group is cancelled and the command is refused with the error of the provision
    Note over GW: Record the task<br/>proof.run · running
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent and the group; the Gateway closes it when the group has ended
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    GW->>SW: Provision the VM<br/>operation-task-provision
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the full provision intent of the group, as for `tasks:provision`
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Admit the cases<br/>tasks.script
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - when the provision succeeded, admits `tasks.script` for the group
    %%> - on any other end of the provision, skips to the cancel; every case ends `unrun`
    GW->>SW: Run the cases<br/>operation-task-script
    SW->>S: Verify<br/>bin/proof-fleet verify
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - one blocking ssh command in the VM: resets the nested test fleet, runs each selected case in order and prints one JSON line with a verdict for each
    %%> - a case exits 0 (passed), 1 (failed) or 2 (unrun) and removes what it created
    %%> - the case phase has a budget of 30 minutes; the reset comes on top of it
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>output tail
    Note over GW: Record the verdicts<br/>last line of the output
    %%> Result:
    %%> - each case is `passed`, `failed` or `unrun`; no usable line leaves every case `unrun`
    %%> - the evidence directory in the VM is kept in the result
    Note over GW: Cancel the group<br/>tasks.cancel
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - always admits `tasks.cancel`, whatever the cases did; it destroys the VM and its workspace
    GW->>SW: Destroy the VM<br/>operation-task-cancel
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Close the task<br/>verdicts
    alt every case passes
      %%> Result:
      %%> - the task succeeds; the result lists each case and the uncovered paths
    else a case fails or the cases did not run
      %%> Result:
      %%> - `proof.cases_failed` when the cases ran and a case failed or did not run
      %%> - `proof.run_failed` when they never ran, such as when the provision failed: every selected case is `unrun`
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - run the command again after the fix; it is a new run
    end
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
